  "result": "I fixed the bug in `IntRange._clamp` in `src/click/types.py`. I haven't run the tests or added a new one for it.\n\nFor an open bound, the clamped value was moved the wrong way, so it landed outside the allowed range. The code did `bound - dir`; it now does `bound + dir`.\n\nFor example, `IntRange(min=0, min_open=True, clamp=True)` given `-5` used to return `-1`. It now returns `1`, the nearest valid value. Closed bounds were already correct, and `FloatRange` doesn't allow clamping with open bounds.",
